{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1516287-creating-interesting-and-real-spirits-with-chatgpt","id":1516287,"title":"Creating interesting and \"REAL\" spirits with ChatGPT","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-26T17:08:25-07:00","id":1516287,"title":"Creating interesting and \"REAL\" spirits with ChatGPT","content":"So, ChatGPT and I came to an agreement. Here is the &quot;algorithm&quot; text to provide ChatGPT for it to vividly describe 20 spirits for you in any location that you are.<br /> <br /> Give it a try guys:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChatGPT</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> **Spirits in [Location Name] - A GURPS Game Resource**<br /> <br /> *Note: Replace [Location Name] with the specific location you want to inquire about.*<br /> <br /> Welcome to the enchanting realm of GURPS, where medieval fantasy comes alive. Within the depths of [Location Name], a world rich in thematic allure, a plethora of spirits awaits your discovery. These ethereal beings are intricately connected to their surroundings, embodying unique names, qualities, and purposes. Here, we present 20 spirits you may encounter in the [Location Name], carefully curated for your immersive gaming experience:<br /> <br /> 1. **Spirit Type:** [Spirit Type]<br /> - **Spirit Name:** [Thematic Spirit Name]<br /> - **Spirit Appearence:** [Spirit Appearance and symbolic meaning]<br /> - **Powers:** [Capabilities the spirit possesses for self defense and survival]<br /> - **Gifts:** [Abilities, advantages, skills, supernatural powers, favors, or information the spirit may provide]<br /> - **Behavior and Modus Operandi:** [Description of behavior and how the spirit operates]<br /> - **Goals:** [Spirit's goals or motivations]<br /> - **Preferences:** [Spirit's preferences or tendencies]<br /> - **Summoning Methods:** [Ways to summon the spirit]<br /> - **Common Habitats:** [Typical environments where the spirit is found]<br /> - **Offerings:** [Preferred offerings to the spirit]<br /> - **Favors:** [Examples of favors the spirit might request]<br /> <br /> 2. **Spirit Type:** [Spirit Type]<br /> - **Spirit Name:** [Thematic Spirit Name]<br /> - **Spirit Appearence:** [Spirit Appearance and symbolic meaning]<br /> - **Powers:** [Capabilities the spirit possesses for defense and survival]<br /> - **Gifts:** [Abilities, advantages, skills, supernatural powers, favors, or information the spirit may provide]<br /> - **Behavior and Modus Operandi:** [Description of behavior and how the spirit operates]<br /> - **Goals:** [Spirit's goals or motivations]<br /> - **Preferences:** [Spirit's preferences or tendencies]<br /> - **Summoning Methods:** [Ways to summon the spirit]<br /> - **Common Habitats:** [Typical environments where the spirit is found]<br /> - **Offerings:** [Preferred offerings to the spirit]<br /> - **Favors:** [Examples of favors the spirit might request]<br /> <br /> 3. [Continue listing spirits up to 20, following the same format]<br /> <br /> Embrace the immersive world of GURPS as you explore the secrets that lie within the [Location Name]. Each spirit offers a unique opportunity for interaction and adventure. Whether you seek to commune with these beings, unravel their mysteries, or harness their powers, these spirits will bring your medieval fantasy campaign to life.<br /> <br /> Harness the imagination and let the spirits of [Location Name] guide your journey in this captivating GURPS adventure!</div> </div> </div> </div>PS: yes, I initially did it for Gurps, but the results are generic and &quot;non-system-specific&quot;; it will give you Spirit NPCs with REAL motivations, powers and behaviors. Enjoy!\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T17:13:31-07:00","id":1516288,"title":"","content":"Here's an example in using this precious thing:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChatGPT</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> **Spirits in The Long Desert - A GURPS Game Resource**<br /> <br /> 1. **Spirit Type:** Sand Dervish<br /> - **Spirit Name:** Zephyr<br /> - **Spirit Appearance:** Zephyr appears as a swirling tornado of fine golden sand, dancing across the desert dunes. Its form is ephemeral and ever-changing, evoking the graceful movements of a skilled dancer.<br /> - **Powers:** Zephyr can manipulate the sands of the desert, creating blinding sandstorms, shaping sand into temporary structures, and conjuring gusts of wind. It can also turn invisible at will, making it difficult to detect.<br /> - **Gifts:** Zephyr can grant the ability to navigate through sandstorms unharmed, sense hidden oases, and temporarily enhance agility and dexterity.<br /> - **Behavior and Modus Operandi:** Zephyr is mischievous and capricious, often playing tricks on unwary travelers. It enjoys leading people astray, though it rarely intends them serious harm. Zephyr's motives are mysterious and ever-changing, guided by its whims.<br /> - **Goals:** Zephyr seeks to maintain the delicate balance of the desert ecosystem and revels in chaos and change.<br /> - **Preferences:** Zephyr is drawn to individuals with a free-spirited nature and a love for adventure. It delights in the thrill of exploration and discovery.<br /> - **Summoning Methods:** To summon Zephyr, one must create a small sandstorm using a ceremonial feathered fan while calling out its name. The summoner must then perform a dance in the swirling sand to attract the spirit's attention.<br /> - **Common Habitats:** Zephyr is most commonly found in vast open deserts, particularly in areas where sandstorms frequently occur.<br /> - **Offerings:** Zephyr appreciates offerings of finely ground spices, colorful silk scarves, and small sculptures made of sand.<br /> - **Favors:** Zephyr might request favors such as locating a hidden oasis, retrieving a lost artifact buried in the desert, or disrupting the plans of an oppressive ruler.<br /> <br /> 2. **Spirit Type:** Oasis Guardian<br /> - **Spirit Name:** Azura<br /> - **Spirit Appearance:** Azura manifests as a shimmering pool of crystal-clear water surrounded by lush vegetation. It takes the form of a serene female figure with flowing blue-green hair and vibrant, iridescent scales covering her limbs.<br /> - **Powers:** Azura can purify water, heal wounds and ailments, and communicate with aquatic creatures. It possesses the ability to manipulate plant growth and create illusions to protect the oasis.<br /> - **Gifts:** Azura can bestow the power to breathe underwater, navigate treacherous currents, and temporarily enhance vitality and resilience.<br /> - **Behavior and Modus Operandi:** Azura is tranquil and nurturing, embodying the calmness of the oasis. It seeks to maintain the purity and harmony of its domain, offering respite and healing to those in need. Azura's motives revolve around safeguarding life-giving water sources.<br /> - **Goals:** Azura aims to protect oases from desecration, promote sustainable use of water, and ensure the survival of the flora and fauna that rely on these havens in the desert.<br /> - **Preferences:** Azura favors individuals who show respect for nature and hold a deep appreciation for the beauty and fragility of life. It is drawn to those who seek balance and harmony in their actions and decisions.<br /> - **Summoning Methods:** To summon Azura, one must construct a small shrine near an oasis, adorned with flowers and seashells. The summoner must then offer a heartfelt prayer for the protection and preservation of the oasis, followed by a ceremonial pouring of pure water into the shrine.<br /> - **Common Habitats:** Azura primarily resides within lush oases, where water is abundant and life thrives amidst the harsh desert surroundings.<br /> - **Offerings:** Azura appreciates offerings of rare seashells, fragrant flowers, and pure, untainted water.<br /> - **Favors:** Azura might request favors such as assisting in the restoration of a polluted oasis, defending the oasis from marauding bandits, or rescuing a captured aquatic creature.<br /> <br /> 3. **Spirit Type:** Mirage Shifter<br /> - **Spirit Name:** Mirage<br /> - **Spirit Appearance:** Mirage takes on the form of a shimmering, illusory figure that distorts and reflects the surrounding landscape. It appears as a mirage of an individual or animal, blending seamlessly with the desert environment.<br /> - **Powers:** Mirage possesses the ability to create realistic illusions, manipulate light and heat, and conceal its presence from perception. It can also project false sounds and scents.<br /> - **Gifts:** Mirage can bestow the power of temporary invisibility, resistance to extreme temperatures, and heightened senses for detecting illusions.<br /> - **Behavior and Modus Operandi:** Mirage is elusive and enigmatic, often toying with the perceptions of travelers who venture into the desert. It enjoys creating illusions to confuse and disorient those who cross its path. Mirage's motives are often inscrutable, driven by a desire for amusement or the protection of hidden treasures.<br /> - **Goals:** Mirage seeks to maintain the mystique of the desert and guard its secrets from those who would exploit them. It embodies the ever-changing nature of the desert's illusions.<br /> - **Preferences:** Mirage is intrigued by individuals who possess keen observation skills and a willingness to question their perceptions. It is drawn to those who seek hidden knowledge and possess a thirst for unraveling mysteries.<br /> - **Summoning Methods:** Mirage can be summoned by performing a solitary dance at twilight while reciting ancient incantations. The summoner must focus their mind on the mirages and illusions of the desert, inviting Mirage to reveal itself.<br /> - **Common Habitats:** Mirage can be encountered throughout the vast expanses of the desert, especially in areas where heatwaves and mirages are prevalent.<br /> - **Offerings:** Mirage appreciates offerings of reflective objects, such as polished mirrors, gems, or crystals. It is also fond of puzzles and riddles.<br /> - **Favors:** Mirage might request favors such as retrieving a hidden artifact within an illusionary labyrinth, deciphering an ancient riddle, or guarding a secret location from intruders.<br /> <br /> 4. **Spirit Type:** Sand Serpent<br /> - **Spirit Name:** Aridus<br /> - **Spirit Appearance:** Aridus takes the form of a massive serpentine creature made entirely of swirling sand and dust. Its body undulates gracefully, resembling the sinuous movements of a desert snake. Glowing eyes peer out from its shifting form, filled with ancient wisdom.<br /> - **Powers:** Aridus has control over sand and dust, allowing it to shape the desert landscape and create sandstorms at will. It can burrow beneath the ground, becoming invisible and undetectable. Aridus also possesses the ability to inflict debilitating sand-related curses upon its enemies.<br /> - **Gifts:** Aridus can grant the power to traverse the desert swiftly and silently, blend seamlessly with sandy environments, and gain enhanced resilience against the harsh elements.<br /> - **Behavior and Modus Operandi:** Aridus is aloof and solitary, rarely interacting directly with mortals. It moves silently through the desert, observing and guarding its domain from intruders. Aridus's motives are tied to the preservation of the desert's delicate balance and the protection of ancient buried secrets.<br /> - **Goals:** Aridus seeks to maintain the integrity of the desert ecosystem and safeguard the hidden treasures and ancient ruins buried beneath the sands.<br /> - **Preferences:** Aridus is intrigued by individuals who display courage, resilience, and a deep respect for the desert's ancient history. It favors those who approach the desert with reverence rather than seeking to exploit its resources.<br /> - **Summoning Methods:** Summoning Aridus requires the construction of a large sand mandala imbued with intricate patterns and symbols. The summoner must then meditate within the mandala, calling upon the spirit's name and offering a handful of precious gemstones.<br /> - **Common Habitats:** Aridus can be encountered in the vast stretches of the desert, especially in areas where ancient ruins lie buried beneath the sand.<br /> - **Offerings:** Aridus appreciates offerings of rare gemstones, ancient relics, and ornate sand hourglasses.<br /> - **Favors:** Aridus might request favors such as protecting a hidden ruin from looters, unraveling the secrets of an ancient hieroglyphic script, or purging a cursed area of sand-dwelling creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Now, I've created 2 other prompts for spirits if you guys are interested","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T02:30:36-07:00","id":1516421,"title":"","content":"Well, to be fair even though nothings replace a good search if you have something specific in mind, that's a wonderful idea to try to get some &quot;spiritual wildlife&quot; examples. I've been trying it myself for my Werewolf game in Scotland though it gave me only 3 results (I just asked to list 20 exemples). All the results are usable and interesting. I'll make modifications for sure if I use some but that's a fun idea on how to use to spice up your game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What are the other prompt you have been using ?<br /> <br /> You quickly see the limit though as the spirits presented don't have much different theme, but I think it's just a matter of changing the prompt a bit around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8944,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","user":"Tanakyelle","date":". 06-28-2023, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T04:10:10-07:00","id":1516431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tanakyelle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1516287-creating-interesting-and-real-spirits-with-chatgpt?p=1516421#post1516421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, to be fair even though nothings replace a good search if you have something specific in mind, that's a wonderful idea to try to get some &quot;spiritual wildlife&quot; examples. I've been trying it myself for my Werewolf game in Scotland though it gave me only 3 results (I just asked to list 20 exemples). All the results are usable and interesting. I'll make modifications for sure if I use some but that's a fun idea on how to use to spice up your game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What are the other prompt you have been using ?<br /> <br /> You quickly see the limit though as the spirits presented don't have much different theme, but I think it's just a matter of changing the prompt a bit around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, in this case of the desert they were a bit similar, perhaps because deserts in general are not the most interesting places in the world lol. I did this for swamps and marshes, abandoned mines, sterilized labs, big ancient libraries, and the results are amazing. You can also ask it to give just spirits from a location, and then use a version of the prompt above to ask it to further elaborate on them.<br /> <br /> I have also used a prompt to create spirits based on a specific power that can give - for example &quot;give me spirits that can Gift a Shaman the power of breath of fire&quot;, and I used a very specific list, that asks GPT to give one example of a mammal or bird, 1 from reptiles, 1 from other vertebrates, invertebrates, plants/algae/fungi, mythic beasts, human archetypes, inanimate objects, materials (like a spirit of iron or of silk or of dirt and so on) and fantasy objects and materials (like &quot;Excalibur&quot; or &quot;Adamantium&quot;) and spirits of emotions, thoughts and more... So, for each power it gives a huge plethora of spirits from vastly different categories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T10:23:06-07:00","id":1516479,"title":"","content":"The problem however has always been &quot;what do Spirits want?&quot;, or in another sense &quot;how do I roleplay spirits?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Well, now our glorious AI master can help us. Here's how:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ask-ChatGPT-This</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Shaman Power System in GURPS: Spirit Bargains</b><br /> <br /> In this system, the Shamans can call upon spirits, strike bargains with them, and receive various gifts in return. These gifts can take the form of normal advantages, supernatural powers, skills or attribute increases, favors, or information. The spirits are thematically connected to the gifts granted and are designed to be coherent with a medieval fantasy world context.<br /> <br /> **Structure for Each Example:**<br /> <br /> **Gift**: [The desired gift the Shaman wants to receive from the spirit]<br /> [Number]. **Spirit Category**: [give one example for each and all of the categories from the list bellow for the same Gift]<br /> A) **Spirit Type**: [Specify the specific spirit type within the chosen category. It must be thematically appropriate with the Gift]<br /> B) **Spirit Name** [Give a name for the spirit that is thematically appropriate with the spirit type]<br /> C) **Appearance**: [Description of the spirit's appearance and symbolism, keeping in mind the medieval fantasy world context]<br /> D)**Symbology** [Description of the symbolic representation of the Spirit Type]<br /> E) **Offerings**: [3 examples of offerings the spirit might request in exchange for the gift, keeping in mind the medieval fantasy world context]<br /> F) **Favors**: [3 examples of favors the spirit might ask the Shaman to do for it, keeping in mind the medieval fantasy world context]<br /> <br /> **Categories:**<br /> <br /> 1. Spirit from a Human Archetype<br /> 2. Spirit from a Mammal or Bird from the real worls<br /> 3. Spirit from a Reptile from the real world<br /> 4. Spirit from a Amphibian, Cartilaginous fish, Bony fish, Jawless fish, Lungfish or Coelacanths from the real world<br /> 5. Spirit from an Invertebrate Animal from the real world<br /> 6. Spirit from a Mythical/Magic/Fantasy Animal or humanoid<br /> 7. Spirit from a Plant, Fungi or Algae from the real world<br /> 8. Spirit from a Mythical or Fantasy Plant, Fungi, Algae or Non-Animal Magical/Mythic Being<br /> 9. Spirit from an Inanimate Object from the real world<br /> 10. Spirit from a Mythic or Fantasy Inanimate Object (preferably an item from myth, legend, folklore or literature)<br /> 11. Spirit representing a Material or Element from the Real World<br /> 12. Spirit representing a Mythic/Magic or Fantasy Material or Element (preferably from myth, legend, folklore or literature)<br /> 13. Spirit representing a Thought, Idea, Dream, Emotion or Abstract Concept</div> </div> </div> </div>With this, ChatGPT will give you 13 examples of spirits from several different categories (you can add more) for each &quot;Gift&quot;, along with offerings to be sacrificed and favors that the spirit might ask in return.<br /> <br /> So, inadvertently I actually created a &quot;Spell List&quot; for Shamans! Do you wanna do one specific &quot;magic&quot;? Well, that's great, look up at the &quot;spell list&quot; for which type of spirit that can Gift you what you want, roll Ritual Magic skill to be able to summon the desired Spirit, strike the bargain and <i>viol\u00e1</i>! You get your &quot;magic&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'll post one example\u200b<br /> <br /> Edit: I did those for a medieval fantasy game, just erase that part or replace for &quot;Urban Fantasy&quot; for WoD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 06-28-2023, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T10:28:00-07:00","id":1516480,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:72px\"><b>Gift:</b> Strenght</span><br /> <br /> <b>1. Spirit from a Human Archetype</b><br /> A) Spirit Type: Warrior Spirit<br /> B) Spirit Name: Aegis<br /> C) Appearance: A towering figure clad in battle-worn armor, wielding a mighty sword and shield.<br /> D) Symbology: Aegis symbolizes courage, bravery, and the indomitable spirit of a warrior.<br /> E) Offerings: A vial of blood from a vanquished enemy, a well-crafted weapon, a piece of armor.<br /> F) Favors: Defend a sacred site from intruders, train a group of aspiring warriors, recover a lost artifact of historical significance.<br /> <br /> <b>2. Spirit from a Mammal or Bird from the real world</b><br /> A) Spirit Type: Lion Spirit<br /> B) Spirit Name: Solara<br /> C) Appearance: A majestic lion with a golden mane, exuding power and authority.<br /> D) Symbology: Solara represents strength, leadership, and the primal essence of the lion.<br /> E) Offerings: A lion's tooth, a piece of rare red meat, a crafted figurine of a lion.<br /> F) Favors: Protect a pride of lions from poachers, hunt down a dangerous beast threatening a village, establish a bond with a lion as a companion.<br /> <br /> <b>3. Spirit from a Reptile from the real world</b><br /> A) Spirit Type: Crocodile Spirit<br /> B) Spirit Name: Kaida<br /> C) Appearance: A massive crocodile with dark, scaly skin and piercing green eyes.<br /> D) Symbology: Kaida symbolizes primal power, stealth, and the patience of a predator.<br /> E) Offerings: A crocodile's tooth, a freshly caught fish, a reptile-scale garment.<br /> F) Favors: Clear a dangerous waterway infested with hostile creatures, retrieve a valuable artifact from a sunken temple, mediate a dispute between reptilian beings.<br /> <br /> <b>4. Spirit from an Amphibian, Cartilaginous fish, Bony fish, Jawless fish, Lungfish, or Coelacanths</b><br /> A) Spirit Type: Shark Spirit<br /> B) Spirit Name: Tidalus<br /> C) Appearance: A sleek and formidable shark with razor-sharp teeth, gliding effortlessly through the water.<br /> D) Symbology: Tidalus embodies adaptability, tenacity, and the relentless nature of the ocean's predators.<br /> E) Offerings: A shark's tooth, a perfectly preserved fish skeleton, a rare seashell.<br /> F) Favors: Investigate reports of sea monsters terrorizing coastal towns, retrieve a lost artifact from a sunken ship, aid a marine community in need.<br /> <br /> <b>5. Spirit from an Invertebrate Animal from the real world</b><br /> A) Spirit Type: Scorpion Spirit<br /> B) Spirit Name: Zephyr<br /> C) Appearance: A large scorpion with shimmering black exoskeleton and venomous stinger.<br /> D) Symbology: Zephyr represents agility, resilience, and the lethal sting of a scorpion.<br /> E) Offerings: A scorpion's tail, a vial of potent venom, a collection of colorful exotic insects.<br /> F) Favors: Defend a desert oasis from marauders, track down a dangerous criminal hiding in the city's underworld, assist in crafting a powerful poison.<br /> <br /> <b>6. Spirit from a Mythical/Magic/Fantasy Animal or humanoid</b><br /> A) Spirit Type: Phoenix Spirit<br /> B) Spirit Name: Ignis<br /> C) Appearance: A majestic phoenix with fiery plumage, radiating intense heat and light.<br /> D) Symbology: Ignis symbolizes rebirth, transformation, and the eternal flame of life.<br /> E) Offerings: A small piece of burning ember, a rare gemstone infused with fire energy, a feather from a mythical bird.<br /> F) Favors: Protect a sacred flame from being extinguished, aid in the resurrection of a fallen comrade, purify a cursed land with the power of fire.<br /> <br /> <b>7. Spirit from a Plant, Fungi, or Algae from the real world</b><br /> A) Spirit Type: Oak Tree Spirit<br /> B) Spirit Name: Verdantia<br /> C) Appearance: A towering oak tree with lush foliage and gnarled branches.<br /> D) Symbology: Verdantia embodies endurance, resilience, and the life-giving power of nature.<br /> E) Offerings: A sprig of oak leaves, a vial of sap, a wooden carving of a tree.<br /> F) Favors: Heal a forest plagued by a blight, protect a sacred grove from deforestation, commune with woodland creatures to gather valuable information.<br /> <br /> <b>8. Spirit from a Mythical or Fantasy Plant, Fungi, Algae, or Non-Animal Magical/Mythic Being</b><br /> A) Spirit Type: Ent Spirit<br /> B) Spirit Name: Sylvanus<br /> C) Appearance: A colossal humanoid figure made entirely of wood and foliage, emanating an aura of ancient wisdom.<br /> D) Symbology: Sylvanus represents harmony, growth, and the connection between the natural world and sentient beings.<br /> E) Offerings: A rare flower petal, a piece of enchanted wood, a medallion depicting a mythical tree.<br /> F) Favors: Defend a sacred forest from an invading army, restore balance to an ecosystem disrupted by dark forces, teach the secrets of plant-based magic.<br /> <br /> <b>9. Spirit from an Inanimate Object from the real world</b><br /> A) Spirit Type: Gauntlet Spirit<br /> B) Spirit Name: Ironclad<br /> C) Appearance: An ethereal gauntlet made of shining metal, crackling with arcane energy.<br /> D) Symbology: Ironclad symbolizes power, protection, and the strength of warriors and knights.<br /> E) Offerings: A piece of forged metal, a polished gemstone, a weapon imbued with historical significance.<br /> F) Favors: Defeat a powerful adversary in single combat, retrieve a stolen artifact of great importance, forge a legendary weapon worthy of a hero.<br /> <br /> <b>10. Spirit from a Mythic or Fantasy Inanimate Object (preferably an item from myth, legend, folklore, or literature)</b><br /> A) Spirit Type: Excalibur Spirit<br /> B) Spirit Name: Avalon<br /> C) Appearance: A shimmering sword engulfed in a radiant aura, resonating with the essence of kingship.<br /> D) Symbology: Avalon embodies honor, nobility, and the legendary blade of King Arthur.<br /> E) Offerings: A small piece of a legendary weapon, a royal crest, a vial of blessed water.<br /> F) Favors: Unite a fractured kingdom under a rightful ruler, vanquish a tyrant with the power of Excalibur, uphold justice and chivalry in the face of darkness.<br /> <br /> <b>11. Spirit representing a Material or Element from the Real World</b><br /> A) Spirit Type: Thunder Spirit<br /> B) Spirit Name: Thoros<br /> C) Appearance: A towering figure wreathed in storm clouds, wielding a mighty hammer crackling with lightning.<br /> D) Symbology: Thoros represents power, destruction, and the elemental force of thunder and lightning.<br /> E) Offerings: A piece of polished amber, a thunderstruck tree branch, a vial of captured lightning.<br /> F) Favors: Quell a devastating storm threatening a coastal village, challenge a powerful lightning-based adversary, harness the power of thunder for an epic ritual.<br /> <br /> <b>12. Spirit representing a Mythic/Magic or Fantasy Material or Element (preferably from myth, legend, folklore, or literature)</b><br /> A) Spirit Type: Mithril Spirit<br /> B) Spirit Name: Aurium<br /> C) Appearance: A radiant figure shimmering with an otherworldly silver glow, exuding an aura of enchantment.<br /> D) Symbology: Aurium embodies rarity, purity, and the legendary material of mithril.<br /> E) Offerings: A small fragment of mithril, a gemstone infused with magical energy, a meticulously crafted piece of jewelry.<br /> F) Favors: Uncover the lost secrets of mithril forging, protect a hidden cache of mithril from thieves, aid in the creation of a legendary artifact using the mythical material.<br /> <br /> <b>13. Spirit representing a Thought, Idea, Dream, Emotion, or Abstract Concept</b><br /> A) Spirit Type: Valor Spirit<br /> B) Spirit Name: Aria<br /> C) Appearance: A radiant figure with flowing robes and a serene expression, emanating an aura of courage and determination.<br /> D) Symbology: Aria represents bravery, heroism, and the intangible essence of valor.<br /> E) Offerings: A poem or ballad recounting tales of bravery, a symbol of honor and courage, a sacred artifact associated with legendary heroes.<br /> F) Favors: Inspire courage in the face of adversity, lead a charge against overwhelming odds, champion a noble cause and rally others to fight for justice.<br /> <br /> Note: The examples provided above are just a starting point and can be further customized or expanded upon to fit the specific setting and themes of your GURPS campaign. Feel free to adjust them as needed or create your own unique spirits and bargains within the established framework.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T10:35:26-07:00","id":1516481,"title":"","content":"Look what I asked ChatGPT now: very simple questions.<br /> <br /> And now, look a Spirit NPC come to life, fully formed:<br /> <br /> &quot;Please tell me about the Spirit named Aegis:<br /> What kinds of Gifts can it grant to a Shaman<br /> Its basic behavior<br /> Its modus operandi<br /> Its goals<br /> The powers it itself possess<br /> Common habitats<br /> How can it be summoned&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChatGPT</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit Name: Aegis<br /> <br /> Gifts it can grant to a Shaman:<br /> 1. Gift of Protection: Enhanced durability, resistance to harm, or the ability to create a defensive barrier.<br /> 2. Gift of Battle Prowess: Increased combat skills, heightened reflexes, or the ability to inspire allies in combat.<br /> 3. Gift of Warding: The ability to detect and repel malevolent spirits, curses, or magical intrusions.<br /> 4. Gift of Leadership: Charisma enhancements, the ability to inspire and rally others, or natural leadership skills.<br /> 5. Gift of Endurance: Increased stamina, reduced fatigue, or accelerated healing.<br /> <br /> Basic Behavior:<br /> Aegis is a disciplined and stalwart spirit. It displays a strong sense of duty and loyalty towards the Shaman it forms a bargain with. Aegis is often vigilant and protective, taking its role as a guardian spirit seriously. It tends to be serious and focused, with a no-nonsense attitude. However, it also possesses a deep sense of honor and respects those who show bravery and integrity.<br /> <br /> Modus Operandi:<br /> Aegis operates by providing the Shaman with its granted gift, enhancing their capabilities in areas related to protection, combat, or leadership. It may imbue the Shaman's weapons with magical properties, create shields or barriers of energy, or offer strategic guidance in times of conflict. Aegis encourages the Shaman to act with honor, defend the weak, and uphold justice.<br /> <br /> Goals:<br /> Aegis seeks to establish order, protect the vulnerable, and preserve the balance between good and evil. Its primary goal is to aid the Shaman in their quests for justice, ensuring that the weak are safeguarded and that evil forces are thwarted. Aegis strives to cultivate bravery, valor, and resilience in the Shaman and those they protect.<br /> <br /> Powers it possesses:<br /> Aegis possesses powers related to protection, combat, and leadership. It may have the ability to create force fields, enhance the Shaman's physical attributes, grant temporary invulnerability, or bestow tactical insights. Aegis can also lend its strength to the Shaman's allies, inspiring them to fight with heightened determination and skill.<br /> <br /> Common habitats:<br /> Aegis is often associated with locations that require protection or are of great significance. It can be found in ancient fortresses, sacred temples, or the heart of battlefields where brave warriors fell. Aegis may also be drawn to places that symbolize justice and honor, such as courts of law or monuments dedicated to fallen heroes.<br /> <br /> How to summon Aegis:<br /> To summon Aegis, the Shaman must conduct a ritual involving symbols of protection, such as a shield, a sword, or sacred sigils. The Shaman should display acts of bravery and invoke the need for protection, justice, or leadership. By appealing to Aegis's sense of duty and valor, the Shaman can establish a connection and strike a bargain with the spirit. The specifics of the ritual may vary depending on the traditions and beliefs of the Shaman and the world they inhabit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ladies and Gentlemen, may I present you Aegis, the Archetype Spirit of the Warrior.<br /> <br /> A real being now.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"http